{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"852737863170654259","content":"(see ring toss for more details.\nDM, mechanics specifics: Sabrine is working on this for 8 hours, after which she will fall into her equivalent of sleep. I will be asleep before she finishes, so I'll run longrest just before I go to bed, and I'll note the extra time needed. I accept the consequences of 'sleeping' in ferrytown. I feel like Sabrine is compelled by /something/ here, my thoughts are the fae, her patron, or in some ways lost memories of her childhood.\nKukudh is not working on this, purely so that I (not Sabrine, Kukudh will be acting alone) can actually talk to people; if this is a problem I'll make them rest too.\nI'll leave it up to DMs exactly what weapons I get, if they work; all I know is if possible I would like two shortbows, as I know two people who want them. if it works, anyone is free to take weapons they need, Sabrine will take two shortbows for her friends Roy and Ed.)\n\nanyone visiting the Isle of Fae sees a strange sight. Sabrine, eyes void, is painting over what used to be the gamebooths, with mystical shimmering pigments, rebuilding them as they were.\non each stall, she places non-magical prizes - plushies and toys of icons of Empire City, such as Grimlock and the Mender. (and the occasional plush of Kukudh, also.)\nshe also paints some weapons, avoiding those with iron - some shortbows, boomerangs, quarterstaves, perhaps even things she doesn't know the name of - hoping the paint's magic will bring them to life.\nshe is painting frantically, with both hands and even with a paintbrush held in her long tongue, uncaring about any paint getting on her void-marked skin or clothing.\nshe will be painting for 8 hours, and will not respond to stimulus during this time, except perhaps telepathic communication. if anyone needs to pass, she will paint around them.\n\nKukudh, worried about her, is flying around as a four-winged, three-legged, horned pigeon. they may eventually become calmed, and leave to check on others.","created_at":"2021-07-16T13:15:59.519000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"865582540994379786","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
